description:
External review #3. crates/wamn-api/src/router.rs: Compiled/Plan/Expand expose all-pub fields, so a future external caller could build e.g. Compiled{sql,params,columns} with mismatched counts. The safety invariants (params/placeholder lockstep, allowlisted identifiers) are only enforced at construction by Router::compile.

Make the fields private (crate-visible) and add read accessors:
- Plan::{kind()->PlanKind, query()->&Compiled, expands()->&[Expand], status()->u16}
- Compiled::{sql()->&str, params()->&[SqlValue], columns()->&[String]}
- Expand::{name()->&str, dir()->ExpandDir, key_column()->&str, target_table()->&str, match_column()->&str, columns()->&[String]}

NO external constructor needed -- Router::compile is the only producer and constructs internally (same crate, private fields accessible). Update external readers:
- components/api-gateway/src/lib.rs execute()/run_query()/apply_expands(): plan.kind->plan.kind(), plan.query->plan.query(), c.sql->c.sql(), c.params->c.params(), plan.query.columns->plan.query().columns(), ex.columns->ex.columns(), plan.expands->plan.expands(), plan.status->plan.status().
- crates/wamn-api/tests/api.rs: many plan.query.sql/params/columns + plan.kind/status reads (it READS only, never constructs Plan -- confirmed).
- crates/wamn-nodes/src/postgres.rs: plan-kind reads; check crates/wamn-gates.

Lighter alt considered + rejected: #[non_exhaustive] on the STRUCTS keeps pub fields readable and blocks external construction with far less churn, but does NOT block external mutation. Private fields is the stronger invariant chosen here (pairs with the enum non_exhaustive in the sibling bead).
